          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Traditionally, there are two different ways to present
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                One can present dependent type theory with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+type+universes"} hierarchy of type universes
                such that every type is a term of a universe of the hierarchy. Examples of such dependent type theories include the one found in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
                and the proof assistants
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lean"} Lean
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cubical+Agda"} Cubical Agda
            %li
              %p
                Alternatively, one can present dependent type theory with a separate type
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
                and no
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
                at all. Examples of such dependent type theories include the one found in
                = succeed "\u2018s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
          %p
            From these two notions of dependent type theory, there are two notions of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %em univalent type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In the first case, a
                %strong univalent type theory
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
                such that all universes in the universe hierarchy satisfy the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            %li
              %p
                In the second case, a
                %strong univalent type theory
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
                and with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
                such that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
                holds in the type theory.
          %p
            These univalent type theories usually have additional types such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/booleans"} booleans
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+dependent+type+theory"} Martin-Löf dependent type theory
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+dependent+type+theory"} Martin-Löf dependent type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+theoretic+strength+of+univalent+type+theory+plus+HITs"} proof theoretic strength of univalent type theory plus HITs
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations"} univalent foundations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UniMath"} UniMath
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Auke Booij,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analysis in Univalent Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~abb538/slides/2018-02-darmstadt.pdf"} slides
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~abb538/thesis-first_submission.pdf"} thesis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+H%C3%B6tzel+Escard%C3%B3"} Martín Hötzel Escardó
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/cmknapp"} Cory Knapp
                = succeed "," do
